<title>ROMANIA: ROMANIA NEPTUN REPORTS 1996 LOSS.</title>
<headline>ROMANIA NEPTUN REPORTS 1996 LOSS.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>					  (billion of leu unless stated)</p>
<p> Loss					 2.22     vs  profit 672 mln</p>
<p> Turnover				  46.59     vs    29.30</p>
<p> Fixed assets			    45.79     vs    39.23</p>
<p> Current assets			  41.03     vs    26.15</p>
<p> Total assets			    93.93     vs    67.98</p>
<p> Share capital			   39.24     vs    39.24</p>
<p> Total debts			     50.62     vs    29.37</p>
<p>NOTE -- Neptun is a state-run gear and pump producer</p>
<p>listed on the second tier of the Bucharest stock exchange.</p>
<p>Data, reported to the bourse, are in nominal terms and in line</p>
<p>with Romanian accounting standards. The Neptun report said the</p>
<p>1996 loss was a result of penalties on delayed payments to the</p>
<p>local and state budgets, of which half were included into</p>
<p>spending. It said it would recoup that loss in 1997.</p>
<p>($=7,084 lei)</p>
<p>-- Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
</text>
